Ques15:
Every engineering design involves trade-offs. Looking at your own IoT project, identify three design decisions where you sacrificed one
aspect (such as cost, speed, power, accuracy, or complexity) to improve another. Explain whether you believe those trade-offs were justified. 
Ans – I used ESP32 instead of Arduino UNO, which increased the cost but provided built-in Wi-Fi and better performance.
I used multiple sensors, which improved accuracy but made the circuit more complex.
I uploaded data at regular intervals instead of continuously, which reduced power and internet usage but slightly delayed updates.
These trade-offs were justified because they improved the overall performance and reliability of the system
